# Rust async

- Do not hold a blocking lock across `.await`.
- Blocking work uses the runtime's blocking pool.
- Tasks that are spawned store their `JoinHandle` or document why they are detached.
- Cancellation of the parent future cancels the child work unless the design says otherwise.
